      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Develop an algorithmic candidate: build first-ID lookup and each node’s exact selected successor, then resolve functional DAG paths with float memoization/path compression instead of repeated recursive scans. Preserve source semantics: strict positive max selection, first matching ID, input neighbor order, float arithmetic, query order, and `%f` output.\",\"B\":\"Develop an independent parsing/layout candidate. Replace costly repeated `fscanf`/linear ID searches with bounded line/token parsing, compact neighbor storage, and a first-occurrence ID hash/map; pair it with a simple semantics-equivalent successor/cost resolver. Preserve all valid header, query-list, missing-neighbor, and output behavior—no input-specific shortcuts.\",\"C\":\"Research conditional 4-core variants on top of a correct serial optimized design: parallel successor construction, independent query evaluation with ordered emission, or dependency-safe reverse-functional-DAG evaluation. Measure overhead carefully: the baseline is only 12.002 ms, so OpenMP startup, synchronization, and output contention may lose. Never use an unsynchronized shared memo table.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates that independently pass correctness and improve full-program measurements. Compare serial algorithm/layout variants before selectively adding parallelism; gains are not additive. Recheck exact float/output behavior and broad valid inputs, retain the fastest measured complete program, and do not alter harnesses, compiler/budgets, tests, or input-specific computation.\",\"analysis\":\"The source repeatedly performs linear `find_by_id` searches while scanning every chosen path, and recomputes paths for every requested ID. The strongest general opportunity is successor precomputation plus memoized functional-DAG evaluation, with fast ID lookup and parsing as complementary improvements. Preserve the reference’s observable selection and float behavior because correctness is judged against it. The 4-core target permits parallel experiments, but the 12 ms baseline makes low-overhead serial improvements the priority.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"a07d1d644acdd59e1a12cf249f4b34bf9d53d1ea1dadeafe64d7faa92b43c103\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Develop an algorithmic candidate: build first-ID lookup and each node’s exact selected successor, then resolve functional DAG paths with float memoization/path compression instead of repeated recursive scans. Preserve source semantics: strict positive max selection, first matching ID, input neighbor order, float arithmetic, query order, and `%f` output.\",\"B\":\"Develop an independent parsing/layout candidate. Replace costly repeated `fscanf`/linear ID searches with bounded line/token parsing, compact neighbor storage, and a first-occurrence ID hash/map; pair it with a simple semantics-equivalent successor/cost resolver. Preserve all valid header, query-list, missing-neighbor, and output behavior—no input-specific shortcuts.\",\"C\":\"Research conditional 4-core variants on top of a correct serial optimized design: parallel successor construction, independent query evaluation with ordered emission, or dependency-safe reverse-functional-DAG evaluation. Measure overhead carefully: the baseline is only 12.002 ms, so OpenMP startup, synchronization, and output contention may lose. Never use an unsynchronized shared memo table.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates that independently pass correctness and improve full-program measurements. Compare serial algorithm/layout variants before selectively adding parallelism; gains are not additive. Recheck exact float/output behavior and broad valid inputs, retain the fastest measured complete program, and do not alter harnesses, compiler/budgets, tests, or input-specific computation.\",\"analysis\":\"The source repeatedly performs linear `find_by_id` searches while scanning every chosen path, and recomputes paths for every requested ID. The strongest general opportunity is successor precomputation plus memoized functional-DAG evaluation, with fast ID lookup and parsing as complementary improvements. Preserve the reference’s observable selection and float behavior because correctness is judged against it. The 4-core target permits parallel experiments, but the 12 ms baseline makes low-overhead serial improvements the priority.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"ac247b0103da45aaba58fd4979b51bac\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"a07d1d644acdd59e1a12cf249f4b34bf9d53d1ea1dadeafe64d7faa92b43c103\",\"session_id\":\"bb34f01e2e114cf4a59ae51b02823166\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"05b2ebd9bddb4c38fc27895812249a4ddc0f794cb67f581c9fea69a361fab021\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":11335,\"output_tokens\":2453,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2062}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":13788,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
